      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], **the Hub keeps the Anthropic API key out of its own process environment by never loading it into that environment at all.** Instead:\n\n1. **A local secrets loader** reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup.\n2. **The key is injected only into child processes** \u2014 specifically, it\u0027s written into the environment of the spawned Ingest agent (and Query agent) child process, immediately before that process starts.\n3. **The Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated**, so the key never exists there.\n\nThis design ensures that if the Hub process itself is compromised or misbehaves, an attacker cannot leak the credential simply by inspecting the Hub\u0027s environment variables \u2014 the key exists only inside the short-lived child processes that actually need it to call the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 5311,
